        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(acp): catch unhandled rejection from handleGatewayEvent in event callback",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe ACP gateway's `onEvent` callback dispatches gateway events to the translator via `void agent?.handleGatewayEvent(evt)` — a fire-and-forget async call. `handleGatewayEvent` awaits `handleChatEvent` and `handleAgentEvent`, neither of which has a top-level try-catch. If either method throws, the rejection becomes an unhandled rejection.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `src/acp/translator.ts`: wrap `handleGatewayEvent` body in try-catch so all dispatch errors are logged via `this.log()` instead of escaping as unhandled rejections.\n- `src/acp/translator.error-kind.test.ts`: add regression test that verifies a thrown `handleChatEvent` is caught and logged.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Code path**: `handleGatewayEvent` (translator.ts:356)\n- **Environment tested**: Node.js v24 vitest test suite.\n- **Evidence**:\n\n```\nBefore: handleGatewayEvent has no error handling\n  handleChatEvent() throws -> unhandled rejection\n\nAfter: try-catch wraps entire dispatch body\n  handleChatEvent() throws -> caught -> this.log(...) -> no rejection\n```\n\nRegression test:\n```\n ✓ catches and logs handleChatEvent failures (31 ms)\n   PASS: handleGatewayEvent resolves (does not reject)\n   PASS: this.log() was called\n   PASS: log message contains \"handleGatewayEvent failed\"\n   PASS: log message contains the original error text\n```\n\n## Evidence\n\n```\nCheck                              Result\nhandleChatEvent throw caught       PASS (logged via this.log(), no rejection)\nExisting test suite (4 tests)      PASS (4 passed)\n",
        "branch": "fix/acp-catch-gateway-event-rejection-clean",
